Package: maluos-tools
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3, maluos-firstboot (>= 0.1.8), curl, ca-certificates, polkitd | policykit-1
Recommends: maluos-desktop-session (>= 0.5.0), maluos-gateway, xdg-terminal-exec
Description: MaluOS Tools Installer: install scripts for developer tools
 One place to install the tools a person wants on a desk: Google Chrome,
 Visual Studio Code, Claude Code, Codex and Ollama today, each as a
 directory with its tool.json and install script under
 /usr/share/maluos-tools. `maluctl tools list|check|install|open|log` drives
 the scripts from a terminal; the Tools Installer window (maluos-desk
 --window tools, pinned in the dock) shows each tool's state and runs the
 same scripts. System-scope installs run as root through polkit (pkexec
 maluctl); user-scope installs run as the person.
